{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-02T18:26:51Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:eb75554702e0c61a70b419bad53ecc06c9aa08ceb0900bb04cf04ff1a4c9b292","decisionId":"rdec-25ee164ce062341a87c07bdb314a38bc","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:df2973547205cf82e3af518f94ac1aeee53b9a5d574388d9831fa4d58ce04d70","packageIdentity":"epkg-8d42657ffa42785e9f8b33a17ba776a3594f71b31038939f4f5bd2cfdd98d412","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent, with one regression to fix first: inline // comments now parse, but a whole-line comment indented with a non-ASCII space now empties the whole menu file. At head 913e112d, a trailing // comment after content parses (1 row, where quattro c05d9019 drops the file), // inside a string survives, trailing commas still parse, and menu-test.sh passes (130 ok). The regression: a no-break space, U+2028, U+3000, a vertical tab or a form feed indenting a // line, or a BOM later in the file, makes the file contribute 0 rows, because JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 fixes the same inline-comment bug (#13493), so whichever lands second needs a rebase.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
